<h1>The rel attribute, profile version</h1>

<p>This is a test profile for html documents.</p>

<p>In the HTML 4.01 specification, we can read
about
the
<a href="https://www.w3.org/TR/html401/struct/links.html#adef-rel">
rel
</a>
attribute.</p>
<p>Specifically:</p>
<blockquote>
The value of this attribute is a space-separated list of link types.
</blockquote>

<p>This test case considers the word <code>"profileTransformation"</code>,
as:
</p>
<ul>
<li>the only item in the list,
for <a href="profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?only"
       rel="profileTransformation"
    >profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?only</a>;
</li>
<li>the first item in the list,
for <a href="profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?first"
       rel="profileTransformation other"
    >profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?first</a>;
</li>
<li>the last item in the list,
for <a href="profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?last"
       rel="other transformation profileTransformation"
    >profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?last</a>;
</li>
<li>a middle item in the list,
for <a href="profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?middle"
       rel="other transformation profileTransformation another"
    >profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?middle</a>;
</li>
<li>a duplicate item in the list,
for <a href="profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?duplicate"
       rel="other transformation profileTransformation another profileTransformation"
    >profile-has-spaces-in-rel.sxsl?duplicate</a>;
</li>
</ul>



